      "writtenOn": "2022-06-01T01:27:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Would autoconf be considered the \"official\" buildsystem to use with cygwin/msys2?\n\u003e \n\u003e \n\u003e It seems I switched to CMake away from autoconf for libwebp at one point due to the issues mentioned in https://github.com/m-ab-s/media-autobuild_suite/issues/1983 with  linking errors with libtiff, but I can try again with autoconf if I should move back or not\n\nIn general autoconf is the canonical build system for the project, mostly because it came first and fit the needs for distributions. CMake is less tested when it comes to packaging builds.\n\nFor the issue you linked, it looks like a dependency issue for libjbig. msys2 is building ok for me currently. If the build was static then it\u0027s possible some extra libs need to be added to the configure.",
      "parentUuid": "23e4a254_31875171",
      "revId": "0d1b9bc4330701df42c6fa9e0b4f72fe74b25684",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
